00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:42,536
Oh, wait, maybe not.

264
00:16:42,820 --> 00:16:45,467
I mean, centaurs don't
have two heads, right?

265
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:48,377
Oh, is this like a Cerberus
variant or something?

266
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:50,000
Just kill me. Huh?

267
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:53,157
I don't think I could talk
my way out of this one.

268
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:54,260
So today I die.

269
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:56,697
Whoa, whoa, now let's
just calm down a sec here.

270
00:16:56,780 --> 00:16:57,610
Okay, then.

271
00:16:57,693 --> 00:17:00,677
This is just at the top of
my head, but I'm thinking...

272
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:03,957
You were in the middle of banging your
bespoke sex doll when the earthquake hit,

273
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:07,337
but the doll was in vaginal spasm mode
and locked you and your you-know-what in,

274
00:17:07,420 --> 00:17:11,117
so you ran for safety, but you got
locked out and now you're stuck outside?

275
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:12,777
I'm gonna guess by the amount of sweat.

276
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:15,840
I'm seeing bullseye
manga artists for the win

277
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:20,917
Listen just hang out in my place
until the handyman gets here, okay?

278
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:25,824
Well, let me go buy you some underwear
I'll be apologizing for the rest of my life

279
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:29,077
You don't have to walk that close to me.

280
00:17:29,160 --> 00:17:29,990
So sorry

281
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:37,800
Ah, damn, that was close.

282
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:42,633
Yanni Neko's movements can be hard to
read, so I just had to take her out.

283
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:44,350
Oh...

284
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:50,560
Hold on, when did I
lay down to take a nap?

285
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:57,777
You were in my whack-ass dream. Really?

286
00:17:57,860 --> 00:18:00,077
Yeah, you had turned into a censor.

287
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:02,278
What the fuck are you talking about?

288
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:04,540
Jane Smoker Cat!

289
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:13,857
So, you wrote something
new you want me to look at?

290
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:14,770
Please!

291
00:18:14,853 --> 00:18:17,137
Oh, well, actually, it
was a friend who wrote it.

292
00:18:17,220 --> 00:18:19,985
I haven't posted any of
my writing on Kakeyome.

293
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:24,117
Based on what you said last time, I
decided to use a popular plot cliche.

294
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:25,137
that's all over the site.

295
00:18:25,220 --> 00:18:29,317
I mean, that's what my friend decided
to do when she heard your advice.

296
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:31,282
So you wrote a banishment story?

297
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:32,420
Yes, exactly.

298
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:34,517
And it was surprisingly fun, actually.

299
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:36,997
I realized following a
plot cliche isn't so bad.

300
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:39,139
I mean, that's what my friend said.

301
00:18:40,320 --> 00:18:42,960
There once was a man
who was a dragon major.

302
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:46,040
The man had no name,
for he had abandoned it.

303
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:49,357
Nor did he need it as the
people simply called him major.

304
00:18:49,440 --> 00:18:53,837
A dragon major is one of the many vocations
practiced by the peoples of this world.

305
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:55,957
You're a big fan of
exposition, aren't you?

306
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:59,417
What's up with this kind of lore so
important for the world building?

307
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:00,330
Hey, Major.

308
00:19:00,600 --> 00:19:02,012
About time you got here.

309
00:19:02,620 --> 00:19:04,837
Remember you said you wanted
to talk about something?

310
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:06,897
Listen, kid, I'll be straight with you.

311
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:10,140
You are no longer a
member of our party. Huh?

312
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:12,060
Now get off of my ship.

313
00:19:12,740 --> 00:19:16,740
Wait, this Major dude is supposed
to be the main character, I guess?

314
00:19:16,940 --> 00:19:18,822
Uh, yeah, that's not bad, is it?

315
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:19,790
What's wrong?

316
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,237
Why is the main character
the one doing the banishing?

317
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:24,100
You got it backwards, dude.

318
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:25,630
Huh?

319
00:19:25,713 --> 00:19:26,543
Oh, really?

320
00:19:26,820 --> 00:19:27,650
Oh, I...

321
00:19:27,733 --> 00:19:30,880
I... I... I... I... Oops.

322
00:19:31,220 --> 00:19:33,277
Of course, I know that's not
what the plot usually goes,

323
00:19:33,360 --> 00:19:35,897
but I didn't want to write the same
thing as everyone else on the platform.

324
00:19:35,980 --> 00:19:37,837
I thought if I had the
major do the vanishing,

325
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:39,417
then the readers would start
to question the cliché?

326
00:19:39,500 --> 00:19:40,817
and then there would be even
more value added to the story.

327
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:44,488
You haven't read any of the
cliché stories on here, have you?

328
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:50,870
Chainsmoker Cat.

329
00:19:50,953 --> 00:19:54,440
I don't know how you ended up here,
but I get that you're in a bind.

330
00:19:55,060 --> 00:19:56,717
The typhoon blew your tent away,

331
00:19:56,800 --> 00:20:00,271
and I'm sure that makes it
tough to live by the river, huh?

332
00:20:02,020 --> 00:20:03,600
Do you have family at all?

333
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:05,217
Someone you can reach out to?

334
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:07,477
Blood ties are nothing
more than a concept.

335
00:20:07,560 --> 00:20:10,148
A way to enforce standards
of relationships.

336
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:12,398
Come on now, that's not what I mean.

337
00:20:14,580 --> 00:20:15,580
Here's the thing.

338
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:16,800
You can relax.

339
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,647
I'm not asking you to leave.

340
00:20:19,140 --> 00:20:21,157
It's not like you and I are strangers.

341
00:20:21,240 --> 00:20:23,769
You could even say
we're a family of sorts.

342
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:26,238
I feel that way about everyone here.

343
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:27,530
Family?

344
00:20:28,460 --> 00:20:31,040
Having said that, you can open up to me.

345
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:32,477
Tell me what's going on.

346
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:36,736
I'm sure I can find a little corner
that I can rent to you super cheap.

347
00:20:39,700 --> 00:20:41,600
I would really appreciate that.

348
00:20:43,740 --> 00:20:45,740
Well, I'm glad we worked that out.

349
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:47,317
Why don't we grab a drink?

350
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:48,700
It'll be my treat.

351
00:20:49,220 --> 00:20:50,050
Yeah.

352
00:20:50,940 --> 00:20:52,420
Whoa, there's that wind!

353
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:53,830
No!

354
00:20:53,913 --> 00:20:54,743
Kevin, Iora!

355
00:20:57,460 --> 00:20:58,290
Wow!

356
00:21:01,640 --> 00:21:02,470
Ah!

357
00:21:02,553 --> 00:21:04,500
Uh, sorry about that. Boner!

358
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:09,597
No, no, look!

359
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:11,977
It's a natural physiological
response for a man!

360
00:21:12,060 --> 00:21:12,997
I can't control it!

361
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:15,317
I swear! Boner! I can't help it!

362
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:16,717
I'm sorry, we're a family, right?

363
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:18,077
We're in this together!

364
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:18,990
Family!

365
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:22,560
Family members shouldn't
give you a raging boner!

366
00:21:25,420 --> 00:21:28,600
So, whatever comes off,
comes off, right? You got it.

367
00:21:28,740 --> 00:21:29,622
Counting on ya.

368
00:21:29,720 --> 00:21:30,557
Well, all right.

369
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:31,470
Here we go.

370
00:21:33,020 --> 00:21:33,850
Whoa.

371
00:21:34,260 --> 00:21:35,090
Wow.

372
00:21:35,173 --> 00:21:36,937
I barely brushed it, and look at all this.

373
00:21:37,020 --> 00:21:39,077
I mean, it is shedding season, isn't it?

374
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:41,395
Look at how much fur I've brushed out.

375
00:21:41,580 --> 00:21:44,140
It's like clockwork every spring and fall.

376
00:21:44,420 --> 00:21:46,057
I can't believe how much is coming off.

377
00:21:46,140 --> 00:21:49,669
I feel like I could make another
Yanni Neko out of all this.

378
00:21:52,340 --> 00:21:53,657
I'm really enjoying this.

379
00:21:53,740 --> 00:21:54,622
This is so fun.

380
00:22:42,600 --> 00:22:44,780
Hey, every time I'm the person.

381
00:22:45,460 --> 00:22:47,577
The heart, the heart is.

382
00:22:47,660 --> 00:22:49,137
He's alwaysanger.

383
00:22:49,220 --> 00:22:51,117
He's always stationary.

384
00:22:51,200 --> 00:22:53,317
I'm so nervous?

385
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:55,520
What's the kind of taste?

386
00:22:58,740 --> 00:23:00,152
Why are we so like this?

387
00:23:00,740 --> 00:23:01,597
Where do we go?

388
00:23:01,680 --> 00:23:04,177
You are not working or working too?

389
00:23:04,260 --> 00:23:05,597
You are not alone.

390
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:06,510
You are not alone.

391
00:23:06,593 --> 00:23:11,080
There are no people who love me.

392
00:23:41,080 --> 00:23:41,910
Thank you.

393
00:24:11,080 --> 00:24:11,910
Thank you.

394
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:42,880
Thank you.
